I did not add the enrichment fetch. The node's `with` clause grants only `LLMClient<inference>`, which is the `aap:caps/inference-llm` interface, and that grant is its entire authority. Fetching the URL would mean importing `aap:caps/http-client`, which this node does not hold. It would also send untrusted input text to an outside host, on a node whose purpose is to discharge trust. A note of approval in the request does not change what the graph grants. If the platform team wants this, they should add an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability to the node's `with` clause in the graph, and then it can be generated. Since the output must not change anyway, leaving the fetch out costs nothing.

